RED: the legacy discovery path is measured outside the seam.

Why this exists: `src/net_bind.rs` and `docs/network-binding-seam.md` claimed
"nothing else in the crate creates a gate socket". That is false --
`crate::http::request` still opens a plain unbound `TcpStream`, and the legacy
discovery call sites (`runner::describe_gate`, `runner::run_once`, `HttpGate`,
and therefore the `Core.describe` JNI export) use it. An independent audit of
the branch found the overclaim, so it was corrected and pinned by a test.

The probe below asserts the *desired* state (both the hardened advert GET and
the legacy discovery GET consult the binder). It fails, which is the finding:
the legacy GET reaches the gate without ever consulting the binder.

$ cargo test --locked --features android-hardened --test network_seam
   (private TMPDIR=/var/tmp/tollgate-private-be8d64b8, umask 077)

running 11 tests
test the_android_entry_point_carries_a_handle_and_its_link ... ok
test a_network_lost_after_the_write_is_ambiguous ... ok
test the_android_binder_refuses_unspecified_and_fails_closed_on_host ... ok
test a_network_lost_before_the_write_boundary_refuses_the_post ... ok
test a_refused_network_bind_sends_nothing_on_any_path ... ok
test no_injected_android_network_refuses_every_path ... ok
test the_legacy_discovery_path_is_still_outside_the_seam ... FAILED
test a_network_lost_before_the_read_is_typed_not_an_empty_session ... ok
test the_linux_default_selection_still_binds_the_device ... ok
test the_advert_get_path_prices_the_body_and_refuses_without_a_network ... ok
test the_same_seam_carries_advert_get_session_get_post_and_probe ... ok

failures:

---- the_legacy_discovery_path_is_still_outside_the_seam stdout ----

thread 'the_legacy_discovery_path_is_still_outside_the_seam' (1194584) panicked at tests/network_seam.rs:732:5:
assertion `left == right` failed: RED probe: both paths should consult the binder
  left: 1
 right: 2
note: run with `RUST_BACKTRACE=1` environment variable to display a backtrace

test result: FAILED. 10 passed; 1 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.25s

Reading the numbers: `connections == 2` passed before this assertion, so BOTH
the hardened advert GET and the legacy discovery GET did reach the loopback
gate. Only one of them (the hardened one) consulted the binder. The legacy path
therefore sends over the default route with no network binding at all.

The assertion was then flipped to pin the measured reality (`bind_calls() == 1`)
so the gap is guarded rather than re-claimed in prose. When a follow-up card
puts the legacy discovery export on the seam, this test must be rewritten to
assert the binder was consulted -- not deleted.
